.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt FILEES-PUBLIC-LINKS 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm filees-public-links
.Nd FileES public FastCGI configuration
.Pq Pa /etc/filees/public-links.json
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Xr filees-links 8
reads this file.
It does not read
.Xr filees.conf 5
and must not be given SVN credentials.
The schema name is
.Cm filees.public-links/v1 .
.Sh KEYS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic fastcgi.network , fastcgi.address
Listener for
.Xr httpd 8 .
The shipped value is a Unix socket
.Pa /var/www/run/filees/filees-links.sock
owned
.Sy _filees-links : www
mode 0660.
.It Ic backchannel.network , backchannel.address
How links asks
.Xr filees-public-authority 8
for a leaf.
On a shared host this is the Unix socket
.Pa /var/run/filees/public-authority.sock .
A split topology uses a server-established reverse SSH forward with Unix
sockets at both ends.
Raw TCP, including loopback, is rejected; migrate before upgrading.
The socket directory must already exist, owned by its service account or root,
with no access for others and no group write permission.
Use mode 0700 for one account, or 0750 with the dedicated socket group.
The directory ancestry is checked before the sandbox is applied;
the socket type, owner and permissions are checked on each new connection.
The socket may be absent at startup while the authority or tunnel starts.
.It Ic visit_key_file
HMAC key for signed visit URLs, mode 0600.
.It Ic cache.root , cache.ttl , cache.max_size
Independently configurable absolute private cache directory, mode 0700,
owned by _filees-links.
The example uses
.Pa /var/filees-downloads/cache .
Keep the directory on persistent storage outside system temporary cleanup;
exclude its contents from backups.
TTL cannot exceed 24 hours.
The shipped values are 12 hours and 10 GiB.
.It Ic bundle.max_files , bundle.max_size
Hard limits for ZIP requests.
ZIP output is streamed, but all selected leaves first occupy cache space.
Logical limits do not replace filesystem capacity checks.
.It Ic intake_root , max_upload_size
Closed upload-shelf quarantine.
Must match
.Ic upload.intake_root
in
.Xr filees.conf 5 .
Job subdirectories are mode 0770 so
.Sy _filees-state
can reap them.
On Unix, new HTTP receivers hold a per-job kernel lock until publication
or failure. Before accepting another upload, the service removes incomplete
jobs only if their receiver lock can be acquired and neither READY nor
PROCESSING exists. Age alone never permits deletion. Cleanup is opportunistic,
not a deadline; it also releases the removed job's reservation.
Legacy jobs without the receiver lock and all published/processing jobs
are retained. Unknown contents or symlinks in an abandoned new job cause
refusal instead of deletion. All receivers sharing intake must be upgraded.
This does not recover a reaper interrupted during publication to SVN.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/filees/public-links.json
Installed configuration.
.It Pa /etc/examples/filees-public-links.httpd.conf
Ordered
.Xr httpd 8
locations to merge into the existing HTTPS origin.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr filees-links 8 ,
.Xr filees-public-authority 8 ,
.Xr httpd 8
